<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese six-month car sales fall 3.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Portuguese six-month car sales fall 3.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese Auto Dealers</p>
<p>Association (ACAP) announced the following new car sales:</p>
<p>    June 1997	 18,773 vs  18,987 (down 1.1 pct)</p>
<p>Jan/June 1997  112,123 vs 116,266 (down 3.6 pct)</p>
<p>First six months by manufacturers' markets share (percentage</p>
<p>in brackets). Comparative figures refer to same period 1996:</p>
<p>    Opel	 15,620 (13.93) vs 16,562 (14.24)</p>
<p>    Fiat	 14,916 (13.30) vs 17,612 (15.15)</p>
<p>    Renault    14,187 (12.65) vs 15,478 (13.31)</p>
<p>    Ford	 11,732 (10.46) vs 11,949 (10.28)</p>
<p>    Volkswagen 10,349 ( 9.23) vs  9,567 ( 8.23)</p>
<p>    Citroen     7,940 ( 7.08) vs  6,640 ( 5.71)</p>
<p>    Peugeot     6,837 ( 6.10) vs  7,495 ( 6.45)</p>
<p>    Honda	 3,841 ( 3.43) vs  4,005 ( 3.44)</p>
<p>    Seat	  3,551 ( 3.17) vs  3,824 ( 3.29)</p>
<p>    Rover	 2,874 ( 2.56) vs  4,307 ( 3.70)</p>
<p>----Lisbon Editorial.351.1.31131247</p>
</text>
